// ProjectDeliveryS683 — Sprint 683: The channel family joins keel github. Under D0453 (accepted on the human's own words 2026-09-12, brief copy-out) the five github verbs - github-pull, github-ingest, github-decider, github-gesture, github-decision-id - leave the top-level dispatch and become sub-verbs of `keel github` (pull, ingest, decider, gesture, decision-id), each keeping its word after the hyphen and its arguments; keel currency keeps its name because it is CI's name for the unattended pass (D0338). In the sprint 512 shape (D0273): a committed transform rewrites every call site in the same commit as the removal, no alias window, each arm MOVED verbatim into the router with its function and its trust classification untouched, and the pre-fold binary is held byte-equal to the post-fold binary on stdout, stderr and exit code over the fixtures the Rust tests use, including the fail-closed case of an undetermined trust - because these are the verbs through which words from outside the repository become facts inside it. Delivers the fifth and last of the folds dcRemainingCliFamilies names; the dispatch count hardening reads drops 39 to 35. CHANGE.. EXECUTE. 2 pts.
