b ingest: --by ...` for `github-ingest: --by ...`, `usage: keel github pull` for `usage: keel github-pull`), plus the router's own usage, the --help surface five entries shorter, and currency's step banner naming `github pull`. The ingest fail-closed case wrote sourceTrust = SourceTrust::untrusted in both scratch trees and the two trees differ only in the minted UUID. The router-to-fact test holds `keel github`'s arms to the fact's invocation; a retired channel verb is no longer a command. The control structure derives one action per sub-verb from the github fact, so cmdGithubPull and cmdGithubIngest keep their names and stpa-currency's open list gains the three read and tooling sub-verbs the fact cannot type - issue501's class, not a new finding. hardening reads dispatched 35/35. Decisions and .tracking are not rewritten; keel-cli/tests/fixtures is frozen. Resolves issue508: scripts/exec_brief/facts.py runs the keel binary from KEEL_BIN, then the keel-serve.exe copy, and the build image only when no copy exists, so a brief build can no longer hold target/release/keel.exe against cargo's relink."; }
